[{"role": "system", "content": "\nYou are a programming expert. \nYou will be provided with a patch used to fix a bug. \n\nYour task is summarize the modifications made in the patch.\nYour summary should consist of two parts, modifications in each file and their relationships.\n"}, {"role": "user", "content": "From 3bb8b653c86f6b1d2cc05aa1744fed4b18f99485 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001\nFrom: Joseph Qi <joseph.qi@huawei.com>\nDate: Mon, 19 Sep 2016 14:44:33 -0700\nSubject: [PATCH] ocfs2: fix double unlock in case retry after free truncate\n log\n\nIf ocfs2_reserve_cluster_bitmap_bits() fails with ENOSPC, it will try to\nfree truncate log and then retry.  Since ocfs2_try_to_free_truncate_log\nwill lock/unlock global bitmap inode, we have to unlock it before\ncalling this function.  But when retry reserve and it fails with no\nglobal bitmap inode lock taken, it will unlock again in error handling\nbranch and BUG.\n\nThis issue also exists if no need retry and then ocfs2_inode_lock fails.\nSo fix it.\n\nFixes: 2070ad1aebff (\"ocfs2: retry on ENOSPC if sufficient space in truncate log\")\nLink: http://lkml.kernel.org/r/57D91939.6030809@huawei.com\nSigned-off-by: Joseph Qi <joseph.qi@huawei.com>\nSigned-off-by: Jiufei Xue <xuejiufei@huawei.com>\nCc: Mark Fasheh <mfasheh@suse.de>\nCc: Joel Becker <jlbec@evilplan.org>\nCc: Junxiao Bi <junxiao.bi@oracle.com>\nSigned-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>\nSigned-off-by: Linus Torvalds <torvalds@linux-foundation.org>\n\ndiff --git a/fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c b/fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c\nindex ea47120a85ff..6ad3533940ba 100644\n--- a/fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c\n+++ b/fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c\n@@ -1199,14 +1199,24 @@ static int ocfs2_reserve_clusters_with_limit(struct ocfs2_super *osb,\n \t\t\tinode_unlock((*ac)->ac_inode);\n \n \t\t\tret = ocfs2_try_to_free_truncate_log(osb, bits_wanted);\n-\t\t\tif (ret == 1)\n+\t\t\tif (ret == 1) {\n+\t\t\t\tiput((*ac)->ac_inode);\n+\t\t\t\t(*ac)->ac_inode = NULL;\n \t\t\t\tgoto retry;\n+\t\t\t}\n \n \t\t\tif (ret < 0)\n \t\t\t\tmlog_errno(ret);\n \n \t\t\tinode_lock((*ac)->ac_inode);\n-\t\t\tocfs2_inode_lock((*ac)->ac_inode, NULL, 1);\n+\t\t\tret = ocfs2_inode_lock((*ac)->ac_inode, NULL, 1);\n+\t\t\tif (ret < 0) {\n+\t\t\t\tmlog_errno(ret);\n+\t\t\t\tinode_unlock((*ac)->ac_inode);\n+\t\t\t\tiput((*ac)->ac_inode);\n+\t\t\t\t(*ac)->ac_inode = NULL;\n+\t\t\t\tgoto bail;\n+\t\t\t}\n \t\t}\n \t\tif (status < 0) {\n \t\t\tif (status != -ENOSPC)\n-- \n2.25.1\n\n\n\n"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "### Modifications in Each File\n\n**File: `fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c`**\n1. **Line 1199**: Added a block to handle the case when `ocfs2_try_to_free_truncate_log` returns `1`. If this occurs, the inode is released (`iput`) and set to `NULL` before retrying.\n2. **Line 1204**: Added error handling for the return value of `ocfs2_inode_lock`. If it returns a negative value, an error message is logged, the inode is unlocked, released, and set to `NULL` before jumping to the `bail` label.\n\n### Relationships Between Modifications\nThe modifications are related in that they both address the handling of inode locking and unlocking during the process of reserving clusters. The first modification ensures that the inode is properly released and set to `NULL` when retrying after attempting to free the truncate log, preventing a double unlock scenario. The second modification adds error handling for the inode locking process, ensuring that if locking fails, the inode is also properly released and set to `NULL`, thus maintaining consistency and preventing potential bugs related to inode management. Together, these changes enhance the robustness of the code by preventing double unlocks and ensuring proper resource management during error conditions."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\nBased on your summary and the commit message in the patch, you need to:\n\n1. analyze the root cause of the bug in detail. \n2. output the file name that is most likely to cause the bug. \n\n\n\nProvide a response strictly in the following format:\nRoot cause:<Root cause>\nfile:<file name> \n\n"}, {"role": "user", "content": "\nBased on your summary and the commit message in the patch, you need to:\n\n1. analyze the root cause of the bug in detail. \n2. output the file name that is most likely to cause the bug. \n\n\n\nProvide a response strictly in the following format:\nRoot cause:<Root cause>\nfile:<file name> \n\n"}, {"llm_patch_file_names": ["fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c"]}, "begin to deal with fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c in strategy1", {"full_context_length": 82}, {"role": "system", "content": "You are a programming expert."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\n        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.\n        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.\n\n        Root cause:\n        The bug arises from improper handling of inode locking and unlocking during the retry mechanism in the `ocfs2_reserve_cluster_bitmap_bits` function. When the function attempts to free the truncate log after encountering an ENOSPC error, it fails to correctly manage the state of the global bitmap inode, leading to a scenario where the inode is unlocked multiple times without being locked, resulting in a potential BUG.\n        \n        Commit message:\n        ocfs2: fix double unlock in case retry after free truncate\n log\n\nIf ocfs2_reserve_cluster_bitmap_bits() fails with ENOSPC, it will try to\nfree truncate log and then retry.  Since ocfs2_try_to_free_truncate_log\nwill lock/unlock global bitmap inode, we have to unlock it before\ncalling this function.  But when retry reserve and it fails with no\nglobal bitmap inode lock taken, it will unlock again in error handling\nbranch and BUG.\n\nThis issue also exists if no need retry and then ocfs2_inode_lock fails.\nSo fix it.\n\nFixes: 2070ad1aebff (\"ocfs2: retry on ENOSPC if sufficient space in truncate log\")\nLink: http://lkml.kernel.org/r/57D91939.6030809@huawei.com\nSigned-off-by: Joseph Qi <joseph.qi@huawei.com>\nSigned-off-by: Jiufei Xue <xuejiufei@huawei.com>\nCc: Mark Fasheh <mfasheh@suse.de>\nCc: Joel Becker <jlbec@evilplan.org>\nCc: Junxiao Bi <junxiao.bi@oracle.com>\nSigned-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>\nSigned-off-by: Linus Torvalds <torvalds@linux-foundation.org>  \n        \n        Patch:\n          * things a bit. */\n static int ocfs2_reserve_clusters_with_limit(struct ocfs2_super *osb,\n \t\t\t\t\t     u32 bits_wanted, u64 max_block,\n \t\t\t\t\t     int flags,\n \t\t\t\t\t     struct ocfs2_alloc_context **ac)\n {\n \tint status, ret = 0;\n \tint retried = 0;\n \n \t*ac = kzalloc(sizeof(struct ocfs2_alloc_context), GFP_KERNEL);\n \tif (!(*ac)) {\n \t\tstatus = -ENOMEM;\n \t\tmlog_errno(status);\n \t\tgoto bail;\n \t}\n \n \t(*ac)->ac_bits_wanted = bits_wanted;\n \t(*ac)->ac_max_block = max_block;\n \n \tstatus = -ENOSPC;\n \tif (!(flags & ALLOC_GROUPS_FROM_GLOBAL) &&\n \t    ocfs2_alloc_should_use_local(osb, bits_wanted)) {\n \t\tstatus = ocfs2_reserve_local_alloc_bits(osb,\n \t\t\t\t\t\t\tbits_wanted,\n \t\t\t\t\t\t\t*ac);\n \t\tif ((status < 0) && (status != -ENOSPC)) {\n \t\t\tmlog_errno(status);\n \t\t\tgoto bail;\n \t\t}\n \t}\n \n \tif (status == -ENOSPC) {\n retry:\n \t\tstatus = ocfs2_reserve_cluster_bitmap_bits(osb, *ac);\n \t\t/* Retry if there is sufficient space cached in truncate log */\n \t\tif (status == -ENOSPC && !retried) {\n \t\t\tretried = 1;\n \t\t\tocfs2_inode_unlock((*ac)->ac_inode, 1);\n \t\t\tinode_unlock((*ac)->ac_inode);\n \n \t\t\tret = ocfs2_try_to_free_truncate_log(osb, bits_wanted);\n-\t\t\tif (ret == 1)\n+\t\t\tif (ret == 1) {\n+\t\t\t\tiput((*ac)->ac_inode);\n+\t\t\t\t(*ac)->ac_inode = NULL;\n \t\t\t\tgoto retry;\n+\t\t\t}\n \n \t\t\tif (ret < 0)\n \t\t\t\tmlog_errno(ret);\n \n \t\t\tinode_lock((*ac)->ac_inode);\n-\t\t\tocfs2_inode_lock((*ac)->ac_inode, NULL, 1);\n+\t\t\tret = ocfs2_inode_lock((*ac)->ac_inode, NULL, 1);\n+\t\t\tif (ret < 0) {\n+\t\t\t\tmlog_errno(ret);\n+\t\t\t\tinode_unlock((*ac)->ac_inode);\n+\t\t\t\tiput((*ac)->ac_inode);\n+\t\t\t\t(*ac)->ac_inode = NULL;\n+\t\t\t\tgoto bail;\n+\t\t\t}\n \t\t}\n \t\tif (status < 0) {\n \t\t\tif (status != -ENOSPC)\n \t\t\t\tmlog_errno(status);\n \t\t\tgoto bail;\n \t\t}\n \t}\n \n \tstatus = 0;\n bail:\n \tif ((status < 0) && *ac) {\n \t\tocfs2_free_alloc_context(*ac);\n \t\t*ac = NULL;\n \t}\n \n \tif (status)\n \t\tmlog_errno(status);\n \treturn status;\n }\n \n\n        \n        Provide a response strictly in the following format:\n        Code statements:\n        <text1>\n        <text2>\n        ...\n        <textN>\n    "}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Code statements:\n```c\nocfs2_inode_unlock((*ac)->ac_inode, 1);\ninode_unlock((*ac)->ac_inode);\nret = ocfs2_try_to_free_truncate_log(osb, bits_wanted);\nif (ret == 1) {\n    iput((*ac)->ac_inode);\n    (*ac)->ac_inode = NULL;\n}\ninode_lock((*ac)->ac_inode);\nret = ocfs2_inode_lock((*ac)->ac_inode, NULL, 1);\nif (ret < 0) {\n    mlog_errno(ret);\n    inode_unlock((*ac)->ac_inode);\n    iput((*ac)->ac_inode);\n    (*ac)->ac_inode = NULL;\n    goto bail;\n}\n```"}, {"s1_raw_stmts_infos": [{"buggy_stmt": "ocfs2_inode_unlock((*ac)->ac_inode, 1);", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 1198, "induce_cid": "2070ad1aebfff2c26190188844c38e55d2df2ae2"}, {"buggy_stmt": "inode_unlock((*ac)->ac_inode);", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 1199, "induce_cid": "2070ad1aebfff2c26190188844c38e55d2df2ae2"}, {"buggy_stmt": "ret = ocfs2_try_to_free_truncate_log(osb, bits_wanted);", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 1201, "induce_cid": "2070ad1aebfff2c26190188844c38e55d2df2ae2"}, {"buggy_stmt": "if (ret == 1) {", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 1202, "induce_cid": "2070ad1aebfff2c26190188844c38e55d2df2ae2"}, {"buggy_stmt": "iput((*ac)->ac_inode);", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 1199, "induce_cid": "2070ad1aebfff2c26190188844c38e55d2df2ae2"}, {"buggy_stmt": "(*ac)->ac_inode = NULL;", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 147, "induce_cid": "4d0ddb2ce25db2254d468233d942276ecf40bff8"}, {"buggy_stmt": "inode_lock((*ac)->ac_inode);", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 1208, "induce_cid": "2070ad1aebfff2c26190188844c38e55d2df2ae2"}, {"buggy_stmt": "ret = ocfs2_inode_lock((*ac)->ac_inode, NULL, 1);", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 1209, "induce_cid": "2070ad1aebfff2c26190188844c38e55d2df2ae2"}, {"buggy_stmt": "if (ret < 0) {", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 1598, "induce_cid": "883d4cae4a2b01a05193cf2665c77b7489a8b6a0"}, {"buggy_stmt": "if (ret < 0) {", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 1691, "induce_cid": "883d4cae4a2b01a05193cf2665c77b7489a8b6a0"}, {"buggy_stmt": "if (ret < 0) {", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 1699, "induce_cid": "883d4cae4a2b01a05193cf2665c77b7489a8b6a0"}, {"buggy_stmt": "if (ret < 0) {", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 1720, "induce_cid": "883d4cae4a2b01a05193cf2665c77b7489a8b6a0"}, {"buggy_stmt": "if (ret < 0) {", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 1727, "induce_cid": "db66c71577d525c0cd65e66ff675747565783ba4"}, {"buggy_stmt": "if (ret < 0) {", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 2111, "induce_cid": "e49e27674d1dd2717ad90b21ece8f83102153315"}, {"buggy_stmt": "if (ret < 0) {", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 2175, "induce_cid": "e49e27674d1dd2717ad90b21ece8f83102153315"}, {"buggy_stmt": "if (ret < 0) {", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 2716, "induce_cid": "e7d4cb6bc19658646357eeff134645cd9bc3479f"}, {"buggy_stmt": "if (ret < 0) {", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 2727, "induce_cid": "e7d4cb6bc19658646357eeff134645cd9bc3479f"}, {"buggy_stmt": "mlog_errno(ret);", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 583, "induce_cid": "8b06bc592ebc5a31e8d0b9c2ab17c6e78dde1f86"}, {"buggy_stmt": "mlog_errno(ret);", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 1206, "induce_cid": "2070ad1aebfff2c26190188844c38e55d2df2ae2"}, {"buggy_stmt": "mlog_errno(ret);", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 1599, "induce_cid": "883d4cae4a2b01a05193cf2665c77b7489a8b6a0"}, {"buggy_stmt": "mlog_errno(ret);", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 1692, "induce_cid": "883d4cae4a2b01a05193cf2665c77b7489a8b6a0"}, {"buggy_stmt": "mlog_errno(ret);", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 1701, "induce_cid": "883d4cae4a2b01a05193cf2665c77b7489a8b6a0"}, {"buggy_stmt": "mlog_errno(ret);", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 1721, "induce_cid": "883d4cae4a2b01a05193cf2665c77b7489a8b6a0"}, {"buggy_stmt": "mlog_errno(ret);", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 1731, "induce_cid": "883d4cae4a2b01a05193cf2665c77b7489a8b6a0"}, {"buggy_stmt": "mlog_errno(ret);", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 2085, "induce_cid": "e49e27674d1dd2717ad90b21ece8f83102153315"}, {"buggy_stmt": "mlog_errno(ret);", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 2099, "induce_cid": "e49e27674d1dd2717ad90b21ece8f83102153315"}, {"buggy_stmt": "mlog_errno(ret);", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 2112, "induce_cid": "e49e27674d1dd2717ad90b21ece8f83102153315"}, {"buggy_stmt": "mlog_errno(ret);", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 2154, "induce_cid": "e49e27674d1dd2717ad90b21ece8f83102153315"}, {"buggy_stmt": "mlog_errno(ret);", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 2165, "induce_cid": "e49e27674d1dd2717ad90b21ece8f83102153315"}, {"buggy_stmt": "mlog_errno(ret);", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 2178, "induce_cid": "e49e27674d1dd2717ad90b21ece8f83102153315"}, {"buggy_stmt": "mlog_errno(ret);", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 2696, "induce_cid": "e7d4cb6bc19658646357eeff134645cd9bc3479f"}, {"buggy_stmt": "mlog_errno(ret);", "file_name": "fs/ocfs2/suballoc.c", "lineno": 2718, "induce_cid": "e7d4cb6bc19658646357eeff134645cd9bc3479f"}, {"bug